# Keeps docker build contexts (sim/target.Dockerfile, deploy/Dockerfile —
# both build from repo root) small and, more importantly, avoids racing a
# concurrent `cargo build` writing into /target mid-build (a real failure
# seen while validating sim/: another session's cargo run deleted a
# still-being-copied file out from under `docker build`'s context tar).
/target
.git
.claude
/scratchpad
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
